{title: 441 - I Saw One Weary}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Early Advent}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[G]I saw one weary, sad, and torn, With eager [F#dim]steps [Am]press on the way,
[F#dim]Who long [G]the hallowed cross [D/A]had borne, [G]Still looking [F#dim]for [D/F#]the promised day;
[D7/F#]While many [G]a line of grief and care, Upon [F#dim]his brow, [Am]was furrowed there;
[F#dim]I asked [G]what buoyed his spirits [Am]up, O this! [Em/B]said he—the [D/A]blessd [Em/B]hope.

Verse 2:
[G]And one I saw, with [F#dim]sword [Am]and shield,
[G]Who boldly braved the [F#dim]world's [Am]cold frown,
[F#dim]And [G]fought, unyielding, [F#dim]on [D/F#]the field,
[F#dim]To [G]win an [D/A]everlasting crown.
[D7/F#]Though worn [G]with toil, oppressed [F#dim]by [Am]foes,
[D7/F#]No murmur [G]from his heart [F#dim]arose;
[F#dim]I [G]asked what buoyed [Am]his spirits [D/A]up,
[F#dim]"O [G]this!" said [Am]he-"the blessed [D/A]hope."

Verse 3:
[G]And there was one who [F#dim]left [Am]behind
[G]The cherished friends of [F#dim]early [Am]years,
[F#dim]And [G]honor, [D/A]pleasure, [F#dim]wealth [D/F#]re-signed,
[F#dim]To [G]tread the [D/A]path [G]bedewed [D/F#]with tears.
[D7/F#]Through trials [G]deep and conflict [Am]sore,
[D7/F#]Yet still [G]a smile of [F#dim]joy [Am]he wore;
[F#dim]O! [G]what can bouy [Am]the spirit [D/A]up?
[F#dim]'Tis [G]this alone-the [Em/B]blessed [D/A]hope.

Verse 4:
[G]While pilgrims here we [F#dim]journey [Am]on
[G]In this dark vale of [F#dim]sin [Am]and gloom,
[F#dim]Through [G]tribulation, [F#dim]hate, [D/F#]and scorn,
[F#dim]Or [G]through the [D/A]portals [F#dim]of [D/F#]the tomb,
[D7/F#]Till our [G]returning King [F#dim]shall [Am]come
[D7/F#]To tkae His [G]exile captives [Am]home,
[F#dim]O! [G]what can bouy [Am]the spirits [D/A]up?
[F#dim]'Tis [G]this alone-- [Am]the [Em/B]blessed [D/A]hope.
